WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.465
Lesson 0.7.

00:00:02.465 --> 00:00:05.620
Your first DeFi steps (practice mode first).

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.678
By the end of this lesson, you'll be

00:00:07.678 --> 00:00:09.791
able to connect your wallet to a DeFi

00:00:09.791 --> 00:00:12.738
app, understand what you're signing, and practise on

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:15.185
a free test network before using real money.

00:00:16.485 --> 00:00:17.775
Here's the plan.

00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:19.460
First, the key ideas.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.175
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:23.700
Then, your checklist.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.862
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:27.162 --> 00:00:29.531
Practice run: read every prompt, do one

00:00:29.531 --> 00:00:32.022
small swap, then revoke the approval.

00:00:32.022 --> 00:00:35.287
First, Connect wallet: lets a site see your address.

00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:37.322
It can't move funds by itself.

00:00:37.322 --> 00:00:39.780
Next, Sign a message: proves you own

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.007
the address (e.g. to log in).

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:42.972
Read it.

00:00:42.972 --> 00:00:46.912
Some "messages" are really permissions (Lesson 1.4).

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:49.340
Then, Approve: gives an app permission

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.197
to move a specific token.

00:00:51.197 --> 00:00:52.552
Limit the amount.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.452
Also, Transaction: actually does something

00:00:55.452 --> 00:00:57.775
(swap, deposit) and costs gas.

00:00:57.775 --> 00:00:59.503
On top of that, Testnets are

00:00:59.503 --> 00:01:02.662
practice blockchains with free, worthless coins.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.997
Ethereum's main one is Sepolia.

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:06.661
You get test ETH from a

00:01:06.661 --> 00:01:09.042
faucet (a free giveaway site).

00:01:09.042 --> 00:01:11.217
Use testnets to practise without risk.

00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:15.290
And Revoke permissions you no longer need

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.702
with a tool such as revoke.cash.

00:01:17.702 --> 00:01:20.717
Plus, Add the Sepolia test network in your wallet

00:01:20.717 --> 00:01:24.092
(most wallets have a "show test networks" setting).

00:01:24.092 --> 00:01:25.746
One more: Get free test

00:01:25.746 --> 00:01:27.837
ETH from a Sepolia faucet.

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:29.872
One more: Make a test swap on

00:01:29.872 --> 00:01:32.449
a testnet version of a well-known DEX

00:01:32.449 --> 00:01:34.852
(or send test ETH to yourself).

00:01:34.852 --> 00:01:37.199
One more: Look up the transaction

00:01:37.199 --> 00:01:39.477
on a block explorer (Lesson 1.2).

00:01:40.777 --> 00:01:43.242
And finally, Then, on a Layer 2 with a

00:01:43.242 --> 00:01:46.212
tiny real amount: connect to a well-known app,.

00:01:47.512 --> 00:01:50.027
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:01:50.027 --> 00:01:52.367
Priya connects to a DEX on Arbitrum.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:55.922
Her wallet shows "Approve USDC: Unlimited".

00:01:55.922 --> 00:01:59.640
She edits it to $20, swaps $20 of USDC

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:04.598
for ETH, pays ~$0.05 in gas, checks the transaction

00:02:04.598 --> 00:02:08.997
on the explorer, then revokes the approval.

00:02:08.997 --> 00:02:10.942
Total cost: a few cents.

00:02:10.942 --> 00:02:12.852
Total lessons learned: five.

00:02:14.152 --> 00:02:15.612
Here's your checklist.

00:02:15.612 --> 00:02:17.147
Do it now, for real.

00:02:17.147 --> 00:02:19.349
First, I know the difference between

00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:21.792
connect, sign, approve and transact.

00:02:21.792 --> 00:02:24.527
Next, Practised on the Sepolia testnet.

00:02:24.527 --> 00:02:26.665
Then, Made one small real swap on

00:02:26.665 --> 00:02:29.102
a Layer 2 with a limited approval.

00:02:29.102 --> 00:02:32.357
Also, Found my transaction on a block explorer.

00:02:32.357 --> 00:02:35.024
And finally, Revoked the approval afterwards.

00:02:36.324 --> 00:02:37.534
Question 1.

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:39.504
Can "connect wallet" move your funds?

00:02:43.924 --> 00:02:46.469
The answer: No. It shares your address.

00:02:46.469 --> 00:02:49.392
Approvals and transactions are what move funds.

00:02:50.692 --> 00:02:51.937
Question 2.

00:02:51.937 --> 00:02:53.222
What is a testnet for?

00:02:57.642 --> 00:02:59.944
The answer: Practising with worthless

00:02:59.944 --> 00:03:01.882
coins, so mistakes cost nothing.

00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:04.452
Question 3.

00:03:04.452 --> 00:03:05.419
What should you do with

00:03:05.419 --> 00:03:06.627
an approval after you're done?

00:03:11.047 --> 00:03:13.327
The answer: Revoke it, or limit it to

00:03:13.327 --> 00:03:15.547
the amount needed in the first place.

00:03:16.847 --> 00:03:18.092
Let's recap.

00:03:18.092 --> 00:03:20.824
Connect wallet: lets a site see your address.

00:03:20.824 --> 00:03:22.885
Sign a message: proves you own

00:03:22.885 --> 00:03:25.114
the address (e.g. to log in).

00:03:25.114 --> 00:03:27.003
Approve: gives an app permission

00:03:27.003 --> 00:03:28.734
to move a specific token.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:33.084
Transaction: actually does something (swap, deposit) and costs gas.

00:03:34.384 --> 00:03:36.899
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:36.899 --> 00:03:39.502
Next up, Lesson 0.8: Your security

00:03:39.502 --> 00:03:42.104
baseline, and the language of DeFi.
